      <title-group>
        <article-title><italic><tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="genus" reg="Ophelia">Ophelia</tp:taxon-name-part> <tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="species" reg="yangi">yangi</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name></italic> sp. nov. (<tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="phylum" reg="Annelida">Annelida</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name>, <tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="family" reg="Opheliidae">Opheliidae</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name>), a new species from Chinese waters, with comments on the taxonomic characters of the genus</article-title>
      </title-group>
      <abstract>
        <label>Abstract</label>
                <p><italic><tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="genus" reg="Ophelia">Ophelia</tp:taxon-name-part> <tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="species" reg="limacina">limacina</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name></italic> (Rathke, 1843), originally described from Norway, is the only species of <italic><tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="genus" reg="Ophelia">Ophelia</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name></italic> Savigny, 1822 recorded from Chinese waters, but these records have never been verified.</p>
      </abstract>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec sec-type="Introduction" id="sec1">
      <title>Introduction</title>
            <p><italic><tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="genus" reg="Ophelia">Ophelia</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name></italic> Savigny, 1822 (<tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="family" reg="Opheliidae">Opheliidae</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name> Malmgren, 1867) currently comprises 37 valid species (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B58">Read and Fauchald 2026</xref>).</p>
            <p>In Chinese waters, only one species of <italic><tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="genus" reg="Ophelia">Ophelia</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name></italic>, <italic><tp:taxon-name><tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="genus" reg="Ophelia">O.</tp:taxon-name-part> <tp:taxon-name-part taxon-name-part-type="species" reg="limacina">limacina</tp:taxon-name-part></tp:taxon-name></italic> (Rathke, 1843), has been reported.</p>
